.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-2-Clause
.Dd September 7, 2026
.Dt SYS-INIT-CHECK-EXTENDED-HOST 1
.Os sys-init experimental
.Sh NAME
.Nm sys-init-check-extended-host
.Nd run or replay the local EHT-01 trusted-host campaign
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm python3 scripts/check-extended-host.py
.Op Fl Fl plan Ar file
.Op Fl Fl output-root Ar directory
.Op Fl Fl seed Ar seed
.Nm python3 scripts/check-extended-host.py
.Fl Fl help
.Nm python3 scripts/check-extended-host.py
.Fl Fl version
.Sh DESCRIPTION
Run from the source checkout with POSIX Python 3.10 or newer.
There is no installed executable under this manual's name.
The default plan is docs/extended-host-plan.json.
Eight fresh sequential workers each run all 54 trusted-host cases in a fixed
seeded order, with classes contiguous.
The parent verifies actual IDs, order, counts, source hashes and plan identity.
Empty, skipped, incomplete or contradictory evidence cannot pass.
.Pp
Each worker has a 60-second and combined 4 MiB output bound.
The campaign has a 600-second deadline, including capture checks.
On failure the existing aggregate helper attempts one-second cooperative
cleanup,
then forces its owned process group and reaps the direct child.
Escaped descendants, fatal parent termination and blocked filesystem I/O remain
outside these guarantees.
These are local host tests, not native Aether or production qualification.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl Fl plan Ar file
Select a local EHT-01 plan with supported fields, budgets and exact corpus
hashes.
The path is resolved before reading.
.It Fl Fl output-root Ar directory
Parent for a new private run directory; default out/extended-host.
.It Fl Fl seed Ar seed
Replay one seed present in the plan.
The result is labeled replay and is not a full eight-seed qualification.
.It Fl Fl help
Display help and exit.
.It Fl Fl version
Display version and exit.
.El
.Pp
Internal worker and plan-identity switches are reserved for the supervisor.
.Sh OUTPUT
The private results.json records running/final status, seeds, expected and
actual IDs, commands, source/implementation hashes, platform, timing and log
identities.
Each attempt retains separate stdout/stderr prefixes and capture outcome.
Cleanup fields state the scope attempted, not arbitrary descendant containment.
Later seeds remain explicitly unattempted after failure; no automatic retry.
Reports use atomic replacement without a power-loss durability guarantee.
Stdout emits the terminal JSON summary only after final report publication.
Operational errors use stderr.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It 0
Selected campaign or replay passed.
.It 1
Invalid plan/evidence, source drift, worker failure or reporting error.
.It 64
Invalid command-line syntax.
.It 130
Interrupted campaign.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
python3 scripts/check-extended-host.py
python3 scripts/check-extended-host.py --help
.Ed
.Pp
For exact replay, pass a recorded seed with the same plan/source identities.
The runner neither schedules itself nor joins the normal ten-gate command.
.Sh SEE ALSO
docs/EXTENDED-HOST-TESTS.md, docs/DEVELOPMENT-CHECKS.md,
docs/decisions/0147-extended-host-runner.md
